WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.192 --> 00:00:02.605
(bouncing classical music)

00:00:02.605 --> 00:00:04.146
- [Narrator] This is Gila.

00:00:04.146 --> 00:00:05.742
He's a Gila monster.

00:00:05.742 --> 00:00:08.639
The only species of lizard
native to the United States

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:10.157
that is venomous.

00:00:10.157 --> 00:00:13.357
But, don't worry, these laggard
lizards aren't exactly known

00:00:13.357 --> 00:00:16.024
for their ability to give chase.

00:00:21.385 --> 00:00:23.621
Native to the southwestern United States,

00:00:23.621 --> 00:00:25.968
and northwestern Mexico, the Gila monster

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:28.119
is a hard to spot desert dweller

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:31.127
spending 90% of its day underground.

00:00:31.127 --> 00:00:33.850
Squat and heavyset with
a large tail and head,

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.587
they grow to be about 20 inches
long and weigh two pounds.

00:00:37.587 --> 00:00:39.993
Their skin is studded with dorsal scales.

00:00:39.993 --> 00:00:41.732
Black in color with scattered patterns

00:00:41.732 --> 00:00:44.620
of orange and red hues,
they camouflage well

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.190
amongst desert pebbles and rocks.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.298
Gila monsters prey on small
desert animals and their eggs

00:00:50.298 --> 00:00:53.073
by using their acute sense of smell.

00:00:53.073 --> 00:00:55.824
Once located, they bite into
their prey with their teeth

00:00:55.824 --> 00:00:57.211
and don't let go.

00:00:57.211 --> 00:00:59.704
They chew relentlessly
until the venom stored

00:00:59.704 --> 00:01:03.923
in their salivary glands can
work its way into their prey.

00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:06.485
Although quite toxic,
their bite is not fatal

00:01:06.485 --> 00:01:08.376
to adult humans.

00:01:08.376 --> 00:01:11.951
Sadly, the number of Gila
monsters in the wild are dropping.

00:01:11.951 --> 00:01:13.656
They've lost their habitat to housing

00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:15.426
and agricultural development,

00:01:15.426 --> 00:01:17.667
but since they spend most
of their time underground,

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.691
we do not know how many are left.

00:01:20.691 --> 00:01:22.858
This is the Gila monster.

